# Cloudflare Pages routing for the civfix admin / operator dashboard static export.
#
# The admin itself is a client-rooted SPA at out/index.html: all section navigation is client-side
# page state (no catch-all detail routes - unlike community-web). Its one other Next route is the
# developer page, exported as out/dev/index.html. So the only rule needed is a catch-all SPA fallback:
# serve the app shell for any path with a 200 (rewrite, not redirect) so deep links and reloads boot
# the SPA, which then restores its page state on the client.
#
# Cloudflare serves real static files (/dev/, /_next/*, /ds/*, /favicon.svg, ...) before this rule
# because it matches them as files first; the splat only catches paths that have no static file. This file is
# copied verbatim into out/_redirects by the export and consumed by Cloudflare at deploy time (it is
# not served as an asset).

/*    /index.html    200
